{"sourceSha256": "d49d6d92726b48e41d78f30b9a4a43a5f8ad913c56f73e8834cce7a8b77be300", "text": "Date: 28/02/2020\n\nDear Doctor,\nRe: Mr. James Chen DOB: 18/09/1950\n\n| am writing to request urgent ICU admission for Mr. Chen, a 70-year-old patient who tested\npositive for COVID-19.\n\nThe condition started on 04/02/2020, when Mr. Chen presented complaining of coryzal\n\nsymptoms following a contact with a suspected case three days prior to presentation. His\nexamination was unremarkable. He was diagnosed with an upper respiratory tract infection\n\nand prescribed Augmentin.\n\nMr. Chen's condition has continued to worsen over the past two weeks. Today, he presented\n\nwith acute shortness of breath and a severe cough. He was disonented to person, place and\ntime. On examination, he had a high temperature (39 C) and an elevated respiratory rate\n(23/min}, though his $pO2 was 95% on room air. His skin was clammy, and he had severe\ncrackling on lung auscultation. His chest x-ray showed a bilateral patchy infiltration and his\nABGs indicated a respiratory failure with Blood acidosis. As a result, community\n\nCOVID 1? and an ambulance was arranged for transfer.\n\nPlease note. Mr. Chen’s general health ts not optimal as he suffers from Type 2 Diabetes\n\nMellitus, asthma and is overweight. His current medications are Metformin and Symbicort\ninhaler.\n\nBased on the above, it would be highly appreciated if you could admit him urgently to the\n\nICU for ventilatory support.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. X", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Date: 28/02/2020\n\nDear Doctor,\nRe: Mr. James Chen DOB: 18/09/1950\n\n| am writing to request urgent ICU admission for Mr. Chen, a 70-year-old patient who tested\npositive for COVID-19.\n\nThe condition started on 04/02/2020, when Mr. Chen presented complaining of coryzal\n\nsymptoms following a contact with a suspected case three days prior to presentation. His\nexamination was unremarkable. He was diagnosed with an upper respiratory tract infection\n\nand prescribed Augmentin.\n\nMr. Chen's condition has continued to worsen over the past two weeks. Today, he presented\n\nwith acute shortness of breath and a severe cough. He was disonented to person, place and\ntime. On examination, he had a high temperature (39 C) and an elevated respiratory rate\n(23/min}, though his $pO2 was 95% on room air. His skin was clammy, and he had severe\ncrackling on lung auscultation. His chest x-ray showed a bilateral patchy infiltration and his\nABGs indicated a respiratory failure with Blood acidosis. As a result, community\n\nCOVID 1? and an ambulance was arranged for transfer.\n\nPlease note. Mr. Chen’s general health ts not optimal as he suffers from Type 2 Diabetes\n\nMellitus, asthma and is overweight. His current medications are Metformin and Symbicort\ninhaler.\n\nBased on the above, it would be highly appreciated if you could admit him urgently to the\n\nICU for ventilatory support.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. X", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2086.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Date: 28/02/2020", "lines": [{"text": "Date: 28/02/2020", "x": 0.0163, "y": 0.01071, "width": 0.18792, "height": 0.01286, "confidence": 0.962, "words": [{"text": "Date:", "x": 0.0163, "width": 0.05465, "confidence": 0.961}, {"text": "28/02/2020", "x": 0.08006, "width": 0.12416, "confidence": 0.964}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Dear Doctor,\nRe: Mr. James Chen DOB: 18/09/1950", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,", "x": 0.0163, "y": 0.06321, "width": 0.12943, "height": 0.01643, "confidence": 0.925, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.0163, "width": 0.04938, "confidence": 0.969}, {"text": "Doctor,", "x": 0.07239, "width": 0.07335, "confidence": 0.881}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Mr. James Chen DOB: 18/09/1950", "x": 0.0163, "y": 0.10107, "width": 0.39645, "height": 0.01286, "confidence": 0.887, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.0163, "width": 0.03212, "confidence": 0.958}, {"text": "Mr.", 